<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>SGI Universal Priesthood | 16-Week Khemetic–Ifá Tree of Life Course</title>
  <meta name="description" content="SwamiG Institute 16-week Universal Priesthood course based on the Khemetic–Ifá Tree of Life, SGI Pillars, and ancestral spiritual practice." />

  <style>
    :root{
      --bg:#07070b;
      --bg2:#10101a;
      --panel:#14111d;
      --panel2:#1d1728;
      --text:#f7f1dd;
      --muted:#cfc3a3;
      --gold:#d4af37;
      --gold2:#f5d978;
      --purple:#7a35b8;
      --purple2:#bb66ff;
      --line:rgba(212,175,55,.34);
      --soft:rgba(255,255,255,.07);
      --shadow:0 18px 55px rgba(0,0,0,.45);
      --radius:24px;
      --max:1180px;
    }

    *{box-sizing:border-box}

    html{
      scroll-behavior:smooth;
    }

    body{
      margin:0;
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      color:var(--text);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(187,102,255,.20), transparent 35%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 15% 20%, rgba(212,175,55,.12), transparent 30%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #050509 0%, #0b0712 45%, #050509 100%);
      line-height:1.6;
    }

    a{
      color:inherit;
      text-decoration:none;
    }

    .wrap{
      max-width:var(--max);
      margin:0 auto;
      padding:0 20px;
    }

    .topbar{
      position:sticky;
      top:0;
      z-index:50;
      backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
      background:rgba(7,7,11,.82);
      border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .nav{
      min-height:76px;
      display:flex;
      align-items:center;
      justify-content:space-between;
      gap:20px;
    }

    .brand{
      display:flex;
      align-items:center;
      gap:14px;
      min-width:240px;
    }

    .brand img{
      width:54px;
      height:54px;
      object-fit:contain;
      border-radius:50%;
      border:1px solid rgba(245,217,120,.55);
      box-shadow:0 0 24px rgba(212,175,55,.25);
      background:#111;
    }

    .brand-text strong{
      display:block;
      color:var(--gold2);
      letter-spacing:.08em;
      font-size:1rem;
      text-transform:uppercase;
    }

    .brand-text span{
      display:block;
      color:var(--muted);
      font-size:.82rem;
      letter-spacing:.05em;
    }

    .navlinks{
      display:flex;
      flex-wrap:wrap;
      align-items:center;
      justify-content:flex-end;
      gap:10px;
    }

    .pill{
      border:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.35);
      background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);
      color:var(--text);
      padding:9px 13px;
      border-radius:999px;
      font-size:.86rem;
      transition:.2s ease;
    }

    .pill:hover{
      transform:translateY(-1px);
      border-color:var(--gold2);
      background:rgba(212,175,55,.13);
    }

    .pill.apply{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg, var(--purple), #3c145f);
      border-color:rgba(245,217,120,.7);
      color:white;
      box-shadow:0 0 24px rgba(187,102,255,.22);
    }

    .hero{
      position:relative;
      overflow:hidden;
      padding:76px 0 40px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.18);
    }

    .hero::before{
      content:"";
      position:absolute;
      inset:0;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 18%, rgba(245,217,120,.15), transparent 18%),
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(122,53,184,.13), transparent 30%, transparent 70%, rgba(212,175,55,.09));
      pointer-events:none;
    }

    .hero-grid{
      position:relative;
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr;
      gap:34px;
      align-items:center;
    }

    .kicker{
      color:var(--gold2);
      letter-spacing:.16em;
      text-transform:uppercase;
      font-size:.86rem;
      margin-bottom:12px;
    }

    h1{
      margin:0;
      font-size:clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.4rem);
      line-height:.96;
      letter-spacing:.02em;
      color:#fff7dc;
      text-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(212,175,55,.18);
    }

    .subtitle{
      margin:18px 0 0;
      color:var(--muted);
      font-size:1.18rem;
      max-width:780px;
    }

    .hero-buttons{
      display:flex;
      flex-wrap:wrap;
      gap:12px;
      margin-top:26px;
    }

    .btn{
      display:inline-flex;
      align-items:center;
      justify-content:center;
      min-height:46px;
      padding:12px 18px;
      border-radius:999px;
      border:1px solid var(--line);
      background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);
      color:var(--text);
      font-weight:bold;
      transition:.2s ease;
    }

    .btn:hover{
      transform:translateY(-2px);
      border-color:var(--gold2);
      box-shadow:0 14px 28px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
    }

    .btn.primary{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold2), var(--gold));
      color:#1a0f05;
      border-color:#ffe7a0;
    }

    .hero-card{
      background:
        linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.07), rgba(255,255,255,.025)),
        radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(212,175,55,.18), transparent 40%);
      border:1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius:var(--radius);
      padding:24px;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);
    }

    .hero-card img{
      width:100%;
      border-radius:18px;
      border:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.4);
      box-shadow:0 18px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.38);
      display:block;
      background:#f7e9c6;
    }

    .caption{
      color:var(--muted);
      font-size:.88rem;
      text-align:center;
      margin-top:12px;
    }

    section{
      padding:52px 0;
    }

    .section-title{
      display:flex;
      align-items:flex-end;
      justify-content:space-between;
      gap:20px;
      margin-bottom:22px;
    }

    .section-title h2{
      margin:0;
      font-size:clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
      color:#fff3c2;
    }

    .section-title p{
      margin:0;
      color:var(--muted);
      max-width:620px;
    }

    .overview{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap:16px;
    }

    .info-card{
      border:1px solid var(--line);
      background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.06), rgba(255,255,255,.025));
      border-radius:var(--radius);
      padding:20px;
      box-shadow:0 12px 35px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
    }

    .info-card h3{
      margin:0 0 10px;
      color:var(--gold2);
      font-size:1.25rem;
    }

    .info-card p{
      margin:0;
      color:var(--muted);
    }

    .course-grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap:18px;
    }

    .module{
      border:1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius:var(--radius);
      background:
        linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.065), rgba(255,255,255,.025)),
        radial-gradient(circle at 15% 0%, rgba(187,102,255,.12), transparent 30%);
      box-shadow:0 16px 42px rgba(0,0,0,.26);
      overflow:hidden;
    }

    .module-head{
      display:flex;
      justify-content:space-between;
      gap:16px;
      padding:18px 18px 14px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.22);
      background:rgba(0,0,0,.18);
    }

    .week{
      display:inline-block;
      color:#160c04;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold2), var(--gold));
      border-radius:999px;
      padding:6px 12px;
      font-weight:bold;
      font-size:.82rem;
      white-space:nowrap;
      height:max-content;
    }

    .module h3{
      margin:0;
      color:#fff3c2;
      font-size:1.35rem;
      line-height:1.15;
    }

    .module-body{
      padding:18px;
    }

    .tagline{
      margin:0 0 13px;
      color:var(--gold2);
      font-style:italic;
    }

    .module-body p{
      color:var(--muted);
      margin:0 0 14px;
    }

    .mini-title{
      color:#fff3c2;
      font-weight:bold;
      margin:15px 0 7px;
      letter-spacing:.03em;
    }

    ul{
      margin:0;
      padding-left:20px;
      color:var(--muted);
    }

    li{
      margin:5px 0;
    }

    .assignment{
      margin-top:15px;
      border:1px solid rgba(245,217,120,.28);
      background:rgba(212,175,55,.07);
      border-radius:18px;
      padding:14px;
    }

    .assignment strong{
      color:var(--gold2);
    }

    .check-row{
      display:flex;
      align-items:flex-start;
      gap:10px;
      margin-top:14px;
      border-top:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.16);
      padding-top:12px;
      color:var(--muted);
      font-size:.95rem;
    }

    input[type="checkbox"]{
      width:18px;
      height:18px;
      accent-color:#d4af37;
      margin-top:3px;
      flex:0 0 auto;
    }

    .table-wrap{
      overflow-x:auto;
      border:1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius:var(--radius);
      background:rgba(255,255,255,.035);
      box-shadow:0 16px 38px rgba(0,0,0,.24);
    }

    table{
      width:100%;
      border-collapse:collapse;
      min-width:760px;
    }

    th,td{
      padding:14px 16px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.18);
      text-align:left;
      vertical-align:top;
    }

    th{
      color:#1a0f05;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold2), var(--gold));
      font-size:.95rem;
      letter-spacing:.04em;
      text-transform:uppercase;
    }

    td{
      color:var(--muted);
    }

    tr:last-child td{
      border-bottom:none;
    }

    .quote{
      border-left:4px solid var(--gold2);
      background:rgba(255,255,255,.045);
      border-radius:0 20px 20px 0;
      padding:20px;
      color:#fff2c6;
      font-size:1.15rem;
      box-shadow:0 14px 35px rgba(0,0,0,.22);
    }

    .footer{
      padding:32px 0 44px;
      border-top:1px solid var(--line);
      text-align:center;
      color:var(--muted);
      background:#050509;
    }

    .footer strong{
      color:var(--gold2);
    }

    .progress-box{
      display:flex;
      flex-wrap:wrap;
      align-items:center;
      justify-content:space-between;
      gap:14px;
      border:1px solid var(--line);
      background:
        linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(122,53,184,.18), rgba(212,175,55,.08));
      border-radius:var(--radius);
      padding:18px;
      margin-bottom:22px;
    }

    .progress-box strong{
      color:var(--gold2);
    }

    .progress-bar{
      width:280px;
      max-width:100%;
      height:12px;
      border-radius:999px;
      background:rgba(255,255,255,.12);
      overflow:hidden;
      border:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.22);
    }

    .progress-fill{
      height:100%;
      width:0%;
      background:linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gold), var(--gold2), var(--purple2));
      transition:.25s ease;
    }

    @media(max-width:900px){
      .hero-grid,
      .overview,
      .course-grid{
        grid-template-columns:1fr;
      }

      .nav{
        align-items:flex-start;
        flex-direction:column;
        padding:14px 0;
      }

      .navlinks{
        justify-content:flex-start;
      }

      .section-title{
        display:block;
      }

      .section-title p{
        margin-top:8px;
      }
    }

    @media print{
      body{
        background:white;
        color:#111;
      }

      .topbar,
      .hero-buttons,
      .check-row,
      .progress-box{
        display:none;
      }

      .module,
      .info-card,
      .table-wrap{
        break-inside:avoid;
        box-shadow:none;
      }

      .module-body p,
      td,
      li,
      .subtitle,
      .section-title p{
        color:#222;
      }

      h1,h2,h3,.mini-title,.tagline{
        color:#111 !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="wrap nav">
      <a class="brand" href="https://swamiginstitute.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img src="https://swamiginstitute.com/swamig.gif" alt="SwamiG Institute logo" />
        <div class="brand-text">
          <strong>SwamiG Institute</strong>
          <span>Modules of Enlightenment for the Diaspora</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <nav class="navlinks" aria-label="Course navigation">
        <a class="pill" href="#overview">Overview</a>
        <a class="pill" href="#modules">16 Weeks</a>
        <a class="pill" href="#assignments">Assignments</a>
        <a class="pill" href="#certification">Completion</a>
        <a class="pill apply" href="#final">Final Project</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">SGI Universal Priesthood</div>
          <h1>Khemetic–Ifá Tree of Life<br />16-Week Course</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">
            A structured SGI-styled course for priestly development, sacred character,
            divination, ancestral responsibility, ritual practice, and embodied service.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-buttons">
            <a class="btn primary" href="#modules">Begin Weekly Modules</a>
            <a class="btn" href="#assignments">View Assignments</a>
            <a class="btn" href="https://swamiginstitute.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SGI Home</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-card">
          <img src="KhemticIfaTreeOfLife.png" alt="Khemetic Ifa Tree of Life course image" />
          <div class="caption">
            Khemetic–Ifá Tree of Life · Universal Priesthood · © SwamiG Institute 2026
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="overview">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-title">
          <h2>Course Overview</h2>
          <p>
            This 16-week course uses the Khemetic–Ifá Tree of Life as a sacred map
            for cultivating source alignment, character, ritual discipline, divination,
            ancestral consciousness, and priestly service.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="overview">
          <div class="info-card">
            <h3>Course Theme</h3>
            <p><strong>Know. Align. Serve. Elevate.</strong><br />
              Priesthood is approached as disciplined alignment with Spirit, ancestry,
              truth, service, and community responsibility.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <h3>SGI Pillars</h3>
            <p>
              Radical Devotion · Words of Power · Infinite Wisdom.
              These three pillars guide every lesson, practice, reflection, and assignment.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <h3>Guiding Principles</h3>
            <p>
              Extending Royal Legacy and Standing on the Shoulders of Enlightened Ancestors
              form the ethical and ancestral foundation of the course.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="modules">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-title">
          <h2>16-Week Course Modules</h2>
          <p>
            Each week includes a core correspondence, teaching focus, SGI pillar connection,
            spiritual practice, and documented assignment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="progress-box">
          <div>
            <strong>Course Progress:</strong>
            <span id="progressText">0 of 16 modules completed</span>
          </div>
          <div class="progress-bar" aria-label="Course progress bar">
            <div class="progress-fill" id="progressFill"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="course-grid">

          <article class="module" id="week1">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Orientation: Entering the Universal Priesthood Framework</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 1</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">The Tree as a map of consciousness, service, and sacred responsibility.</p>
              <p>
                Students are introduced to the SGI Universal Priesthood framework and the Khemetic–Ifá Tree of Life
                as a living spiritual anatomy of source, crown, mind, heart, action, devotion, earth, protection,
                transformation, and ancestry.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Key Lessons</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Universal Priesthood as a path of service.</li>
                <li>The Tree as a sacred map of priestly development.</li>
                <li>The SGI pillars and guiding principles.</li>
                <li>The difference between spiritual interest and spiritual responsibility.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="assignment">
                <strong>Assignment:</strong> Create a Universal Priesthood Intention Statement.
              </div>
              <label class="check-row">
                <input type="checkbox" data-week="1" />
                <span>Mark Week 1 complete</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="module" id="week2">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Amen / Olorun: Source, Breath, and Divine Origin</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">The invisible source behind all visible power.</p>
              <p>
                Amen / Olorun represents the unseen origin, divine mystery, breath, consciousness, and source
                alignment. Students learn to begin priesthood from humility, silence, and spiritual origin.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Key Lessons</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Source before form.</li>
                <li>Breath as sacred connection.</li>
                <li>Prayer as alignment rather than begging.</li>
                <li>Silence as spiritual preparation.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="assignment">
                <strong>Practice:</strong> Seven-day breath prayer.<br />
                <strong>Assignment:</strong> Breath Prayer Reflection.
              </div>
              <label class="check-row">
                <input type="checkbox" data-week="2" />
                <span>Mark Week 2 complete</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="module" id="week3">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Ausar / Obatala: Clarity, Crown, and Moral Authority</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 3</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">Clear head, clean character, elevated consciousness.</p>
              <p>
                Ausar / Obatala teaches clarity, coolness, purity, moral order, and elevated consciousness.
                Students examine Ori, restraint, and the ethical responsibility of spiritual authority.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Key Lessons</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Ori, crown, and elevated consciousness.</li>
                <li>Coolness as spiritual maturity.</li>
                <li>Purity as clarity, not perfectionism.</li>
                <li>Moral authority through right conduct.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="assignment">
                <strong>Practice:</strong> Cool-head reflection ritual.<br />
                <strong>Assignment:</strong> Ori / Clarity Reflection.
              </div>
              <label class="check-row">
                <input type="checkbox" data-week="3" />
                <span>Mark Week 3 complete</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="module" id="week4">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Sekert / Olokun: Depth, Mystery, and Words of Power</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 4</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">The hidden waters of memory, speech, and spiritual depth.</p>
              <p>
                Sekert / Olokun opens the mystery of sacred depth, silence, memory, dream consciousness,
                and the SGI pillar Words of Power. Students learn to speak with spiritual discipline.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Key Lessons</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Hidden knowledge and sacred silence.</li>
                <li>Dreams, memory, and inner stillness.</li>
                <li>Speech as spiritual technology.</li>
                <li>The difference between talking and invoking.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="assignment">
                <strong>Practice:</strong> Seven-day speech discipline.<br />
                <strong>Assignment:</strong> Words of Power Declaration.
              </div>
              <label class="check-row">
                <input type="checkbox" data-week="4" />
                <span>Mark Week 4 complete</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="module" id="week5">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Tehuti / Orunmila: Divination, Sacred Intelligence, and the Wisdom of Signs</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 5</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">Divination as disciplined listening.</p>
              <p>
                This module explicitly introduces divination as a priestly technology. Students study sacred inquiry,
                question formation, interpretation, destiny, signs, and ethical documentation.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Approved Practice Options</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Obi or four cowries.</li>
                <li>Card-based reflection.</li>
                <li>Opele observation.</li>
                <li>Guided symbolic interpretation.</li>
                <li>Signs and confirmation journaling.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="assignment">
                <strong>Assignment:</strong> Documented Divination Report including date, question, method,
                result, interpretation, action, and follow-up observation.
              </div>
              <label class="check-row">
                <input type="checkbox" data-week="5" />
                <span>Mark Week 5 complete</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="module" id="week6">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Herukhuti / Ogun: Action, Power, and Constructive Force</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 6</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">Disciplined power, courage, tools, and sacred work.</p>
              <p>
                Herukhuti / Ogun represents action, force, courage, tools, technology, labor, boundaries,
                and the power to cut through obstruction with purpose.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Key Lessons</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Action as sacred responsibility.</li>
                <li>Tools as extensions of consciousness.</li>
                <li>Boundaries as spiritual protection.</li>
                <li>Work as ritual.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="assignment">
                <strong>Assignment:</strong> Ogun Action Report: identify one obstruction and complete one disciplined action.
              </div>
              <label class="check-row">
                <input type="checkbox" data-week="6" />
                <span>Mark Week 6 complete</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="module" id="week7">
            <div class="module-head">
              <h3>Maat / Iwa Pele: Truth, Balance, and Character</h3>
              <span class="week">Week 7</span>
            </div>
            <div class="module-body">
              <p class="tagline">Priesthood proven through character.</p>
              <p>
                Maat / Iwa Pele anchors the moral center of the course. Students study truth, justice,
                balance, accountability, right relationship, and the spiritual beauty of good character.
              </p>
              <div class="mini-title">Daily Self-Audit</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Where did I restore balance today?</li>
